README.OSK -- uutools (uue, uud) on this diskSource: UUCPbb 2.1 documentation archive, UUCPBB21/MISC/MISC/uutools.lzhand uutools_src.lzh.  ORIG/ holds both archives' contents unchanged,including the two 6809 binaries (uue, uud) the archive shipped.Built with this collection's recipe:    uue|uutools|uue.c|OS9||    uud|uutools|uud.c|OS9||(-qm and -n=<prog> are the driver's defaults.)  makefile.osk names Ultra C(-bc, -fd, -oln); the recipe replaces it.One source change, in uue.c:  - Removed the three lines        #ifdef OS9        #define fputc putc        #endif    With them, maketable() called putc(i++, outp).  This compiler's putc is    a macro, and the translation table came out EMPTY -- "table" followed by    two blank lines -- so uud refused every file uue wrote with    "uud: Incomplete translation table."  Measured before and after; with    the real fputc() the table is written and uud round-trips the file.uud.c is unchanged.